# Weekly FAILED DEBITS report to the Debtors recipient list.
#
# WHY (CFO 2026-09-11): an Accounts Assistant exported the failed debit orders by
# hand, pasted them into a spreadsheet and emailed Underwriting and the agents to
# chase the clients. The export and the email are mechanical; the chasing is not.
# Omni now reads the failures live from Graphite and sends the same email, to a
# recipient list Finance maintain themselves on screen.
#
# 12:00 UTC FRIDAY = 14:00 Friday in Gaborone (Botswana never observes DST, so
# this offset is fixed year-round) — CFO 2026-09-12, moved off Monday so
# Bokani's broker chase list lands before the weekend, not at the start of the
# following week. Day-of-week 5 is Friday.
#
# omni-manage, NOT `docker compose exec`: the raw form was retired on 2026-09-04
# after a cron ran mid blue/green flip and the company lost a day's attendance
# record. The wrapper waits for a healthy container instead of writing into a
# dying one.
#
# Read-only. It SELECTs through integrations.graphite_ro and sends an email. It
# raises no payment, changes no policy and moves no money. It exits NON-ZERO when
# Graphite is unreachable or the recipient list is empty, so a broken Monday
# never looks like a quiet one.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

0 12 * * 5 root /usr/local/bin/omni-manage send_failed_debits_report >> /var/log/alpha-finance/failed-debits-report.log 2>&1
